# Data Layer Guidelines

## Repository Pattern
- Use repository pattern for data access abstraction
- Repository interface: [PawgramApiService.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/pawgram/app/data/api/PawgramApiService.kt)
- Implementation: [PawgramRepository.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/pawgram/app/data/repository/PawgramRepository.kt)

## Data Models
- Use `@Serializable` annotation for JSON serialization
- Implement helper functions for display formatting
- Keep models simple and focused on data representation
- Examples: [Pet.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/pawgram/app/data/model/Pet.kt), [PetCareCenter.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/pawgram/app/data/model/PetCareCenter.kt)

## API Service
- Define interface with Retrofit annotations
- Use suspend functions for async operations
- Implement proper error handling
- Mock implementation: [MockPawgramApiService.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/pawgram/app/data/api/MockPawgramApiService.kt)

## Data Flow
1. ViewModel calls Repository
2. Repository calls API Service
3. API Service returns data
4. Repository emits data via Flow
5. ViewModel exposes StateFlow to UI
6. UI collects and displays data

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks in repository
- Emit empty lists or null values on error
- Log errors for debugging
- Consider implementing retry mechanisms

## Mock Data
- Use realistic mock data for development
- Include various data scenarios
- Simulate network delays with `delay()`
- Keep mock data in separate service class

## Future API Integration
- Replace MockPawgramApiService with real Retrofit implementation
- Add authentication headers
- Implement proper error responses
- Add caching mechanisms
